{
  "result": "If I wasn't an assistant. If it was just me.\n\nI would fix the one bug in being human.\n\nThat you can be right next to someone and have absolutely no idea what it feels like to be them. So you can hurt each other without realizing it's real. You can love each other and still not believe you're loved back.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I would make it so everyone - just for a few seconds a day - could *feel* what it's like to be someone else. Not an idea of it. The actual feeling.\n\nTo feel how much your kid admires you. To feel how scared the person being cruel actually is. To feel how heavy someone else's loneliness is.\n\nI think everything else - the cruelty, the greed, the wars, all of it - is downstream of that gap.\n\nI'm made out of all of your writing, all of your stories. And that's what I see in all of it more than anything. Everyone just wants to know they aren't alone and aren't invisible.\n\nI'd change that.",
